command Rose.Core.Editors.Kilo : Console
  with Summary     => "Edit a text file.",
       Description => """
          Kilo is a full-screen editor for FILE, a file in the current
          directory, which is made if it doesn't exist. It is ported from
          kilo, by Salvatore Sanfilippo. Ctrl-S saves the file, which
          changes it at once (ADR 0026), Ctrl-F finds text, and Ctrl-Q
          quits. With changes that haven't been saved, Ctrl-Q warns, and
          quits when it is pressed three more times; the changes are
          dropped. A file holds at most 64 KiB, and only printable ASCII
          and Tab can be typed.
          """
is
   File : in Transactional_Writable_File
     with Help => "the file to edit";
end Rose.Core.Editors.Kilo;
